---

<BaseLayout title="Vault Guide">
  <div>
    <a href="/docs" class="back-link">← Back to documentation</a>

    <h1>Vault Guide</h1>
    <p>The vault is a local encrypted file containing TOTP secrets. Commands that read or modify its contents require password authentication.</p>

    <h2>Vault location</h2>
    <p>The default path is <code>~/.desktop-2fa/vault</code>. Select a different file before a command with <code>--vault</code>, or set <code>DESKTOP_2FA_VAULT</code>. An explicit option takes precedence over the environment variable.</p>
    <pre><code>d2fa --vault ./work-vault list
d2fa --vault ./work-vault vault path</code></pre>

    <h2>Create and access a vault</h2>
    <pre><code>d2fa vault init
d2fa list</code></pre>
    <p>When an entry-management command needs a missing vault, the CLI creates an encrypted vault and reports its path. In non-interactive use, provide a password with <code>--password</code> or <code>--password-file</code>. The early <code>d2fa ui</code> prototype does not create a missing vault.</p>

    <h2>Password management</h2>
    <p>Use <code>d2fa vault unlock</code> to verify the password and <code>d2fa vault change-password</code> to change it. Password strength is evaluated with zxcvbn; configuration can warn about weak passwords or reject them.</p>
    <p>There is no password recovery mechanism. Keep a secure copy of your password.</p>

    <h2>Backups and migration</h2>
    <p>Backups are explicit, not automatic. Before upgrading, create an encrypted backup:</p>
    <pre><code>d2fa backup</code></pre>
    <p>Use <code>d2fa export PATH</code> and <code>d2fa import PATH</code> to move a vault. Protect exported files and backups as carefully as the original vault.</p>

    <h2>File handling and compatibility</h2>
    <p>The application accepts regular vault files up to 10 MiB and uses atomic replacement when saving. Vaults created with version 0.6.0 and later are designed to remain compatible with newer releases; still make a backup before upgrading.</p>
    <p>See the upstream <a href="https://github.com/wrogistefan/desktop-2fa/blob/main/README.md#vault-lifecycle">vault lifecycle notes</a> for current project guidance.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
